{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms","id":804701,"title":"Uniquely Lunar Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-09T14:22:26-08:00","id":804701,"title":"Uniquely Lunar Charms","content":"Okay so in the hierarchy thread the &quot;Solars are the best at anything, but other exalted are the best at being other exalted.&quot; thing was brought up. I think Sidereals are really good at this. Solar dodge charms let you dodge an attack, Sidereal dodge charms let you move a city around. Solar ride charms let you make an epic and unstoppable mounted charge, Sidereal ride charms let you turn a mortal into a celestial dragon and bomb around on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar charms are technically better at doing what their ability wants you to do, and Neighborhood Relocation Technique isn't exactly going to help you against an orichalcum daiklave to the face, but it's cool and powerful enough in it's own way to really sell people on Sids. Like if you had a friend who'd never even looked at a non-solar charmset and he wanted to know why you'd ever play a Sidreal archer when you could play a Solar archer, you could point to the fact that Sid archery lets you counterattack with a bow and fire things like rain and love and bountiful crops. Yeah, you're not a Solar archer, you'd lose in a fight against one, but you can do crazy awesome stuff that Solars would never dream of doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly, I haven't had the chance to play many Lunars, 2-3 at most I think, and at least one of those was for exactly one intro session. So basically what I want to know from people who've played tons of Lunars, what Lunar charms out there are like that? Or what Lunar charms would you like to see like that in the future? DB charms would also be welcome because I often find that unique DB mechanics are actually Solar mechanics with a bad, sometimes non-existant &quot;No srsly guys, Dragonfly Finds Mate is totally a DB charm and not a Solar one. Honest.&quot; paint job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:01:12-08:00","id":804725,"title":"","content":"While I haven't had a chance to play either, Wind-Carried-Words Technique and Elemental Bolt Attack are probably the most iconic Dragonblooded charms I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:09:00-08:00","id":804732,"title":"","content":"Lunar charms are meant to be more versatile than solar charms - at the same time they're not as cost effective. I like the charms from Glories: Luna as really good examples of this.<br /> <br /> Charms like River Reflects Desire and Dreams and Expectations Stance, which makes an onlooker think the lunar is... something else, or something he expected, even when the lunar isn't. It's not a disguise charm that will disguise you as someone specific, but it can get you into damn near any place if you use it wisely and intelligently. A solar disguise charm would let you disguise yourself as something specific, and do so very well - the lunar one can effectively change who you appear to be at the drop of a hat.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Flesh-Sculpting Art is a really iconic lunar charm.<br /> <br /> Do you need to interogate someone? Just begin molding one of their legs into the form of a kitten and say &quot;I can undo this... if you tell me what I want to know&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you need to fix a wound? Just patch it up<br /> <br /> Grow three feet of hair? Pull it out?<br /> <br /> Regrow an arm? A touch of the wyld and a bit of willpower.<br /> <br /> Its a charm with endless possibilities - or barely any, if you're not the creative sort.<br /> <br /> <br /> Argent Weaver Art is the same story: Officially it just lets you go all spiderman and make string spun of lunar essence.<br /> <br /> But you can make webs, rope, tie things up, tie people up, lash things together, snare people, lasso people, retrieve your weapon. Think of all the things spiderman can do with his webbing... this is now but one of your tricks as a lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> Implausible Lunar Panoply. It might take an hour to stash something, but you can retrieve it in an instant. A grand pile of jade? An implosion bow ready to fire? A guild wagon? A house? A bomb about to explode?<br /> <br /> <br /> Solar charms are really good at what they do - but can't be used outside of what they're meant to let you do. There's a solar larceny charm that lets you walk through doors, only doors, not windows, not walls, only doors. A lunar would just turn into a fly and zip over the city wall, or as a flea go through a lock.<br /> <br /> IMO lunar charms don't need to be better - one just has to think differently when using lunars","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T19:13:33-08:00","id":804922,"title":"","content":"The most uniquely Lunar Charms are the ones that give you partial transformations. Hybrid Body Rearrangement is the wrong way to go in adding mutations; Lunar Charms should mostly resemble mutations but be much more effective, and normal mutations shouldn't be the things they mess around with. First edition had about half of this, with the other half being tied up in a botched execution that wanted to have a difference between tentacles that did bashing and tentacles that did lethal, among other deep issues. Illusion are generally to be avoided.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't count Flesh-Sculpting Art as the most iconic image of Lunars healing others. I think that should be Lick Wound instead, only with better hypothetical mechanics. FSA is really rather deep in Abyssal or Liminal territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T19:25:55-08:00","id":804931,"title":"","content":"I said this a long time ago, but I feel that a big part of the problem isn't just the lack of uniquely Lunar <i>charms</i>; the problem is that the basic Lunar narrative is very close to the Solar one, in terms of how they Exalt. Going over the types of Exalted and how they Exalt:<br /> <br /> Solars are ordinary humans, wandering the world, who are uplifted by their patron out of the blue for excellence.<br /> Dragon-Blooded inherit their power.<br /> Sidereals are fated to Exalt from the moment of birth and are swept up to Heaven shortly after (or before) they Exalt.<br /> Abyssals are chosen at the moment of death and have the option to accept or refuse.<br /> Alchemicals are made (and therefore, generally, tightly bound to the city that made them, at least in terms of their backstory.)<br /> Infernals have their failure thing, and have to choose to accept, but much more importantly they're swept off to Hell almost immediately.<br /> <br /> All of those are very unique and lead to very different stories.<br /> <br /> Then you have the Lunar one, which is basically &quot;like the Solar one, but for a very, very subtly different <i>kind</i> of excellence.&quot; (And even that isn't really distinguished; Solars can be chosen because they're great survivors, too.) While Lunars have a bit more infrastructure than Solars, they're still the second-most infrastructure-light type of Exalt; at least as I've generally seen them used, the Lunar elders don't have the dramatic impact on them that the Realm, Heaven, Hell,or the Underworld has on DB, Sidereals, Infernals, or Abyssals (and let's not even get into Alchemicals.)<br /> <br /> And while the game sometimes tried to make the Wyld the Lunar 'thing', it never really worked out, especially since Fair Folk are pushed fairly seriously as playable, probably more seriously than any other non-Exalt option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-09-2016, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:27:56-08:00","id":805000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=804732#post804732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar charms are meant to be more versatile than solar charms - at the same time they're not as cost effective.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Solar charms are really good at what they do - but can't be used outside of what they're meant to let you do. There's a solar larceny charm that lets you walk through doors, only doors, not windows, not walls, only doors. A lunar would just turn into a fly and zip over the city wall, or as a flea go through a lock.<br /> <br /> IMO lunar charms don't need to be better - one just has to think differently when using lunars</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice, at least half of all Lunar Charms aren't actually more versatile than Solar ones. The Stamina Attribute in particular is thematically indistinguishable from the Resistance Ability, enabling all of the same kind of Charms and very few different concepts.<br /> <br /> However, the Lunar Charmset IS structured very differently from the Solar one because of the Attribute focus. A Solar has to learn Brawl AND Athletics Charms in order to pick up giants and hurl them across battlefields. A Lunar can find all of that in a SINGLE branch of Strength Charms.<br /> <br /> A Solar who wants to be perceptive has to buy up various different Abilities (Socialize, Investigate, Medicine, Survival) to roll with his Perception, and the Charms for each of those different abilities, but a Lunar only needs to invest in the Perception Attribute, which likewise contains<i> every single possible Lunar perception trick</i>.<br /> <br /> And that's before introducing limitations that Solars don't worry about. Lunar effects need to be more internal, with less outright transformation or conjuration of external objects, and Attribute Charm themes need to be limited in ways that Ability Charms don't.<br /> <br /> For example, Clay-Wetting Practice can't return in its original form because the concept of &quot;fuse Essence into an object, then mold it like putty&quot; isn't limited by Dexterity in the way that Glorious Solar Saber is limited by Melee. Obviously, GSS can never be taken to the point of conjuring up armor or horses, because all following Charms still have to be Melee Charms. But what would stop Charms following CWP from exploring the concept of &quot;the Lunar injects larger amounts of Essence into the world to reshape it according to her visions&quot;? That concept doesn't contradict anything about the Dexterity Attribute, so the limitation needs to come from Lunar themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, Flesh-Sculpting Art and Clay-Wetting Practice can still can work, by playing to Lunar themes. For example, feeding your blood to a patient blurs the boundaries of &quot;internal / external&quot;, and introduces the limitation that improving your effect upon the world requires you to work with the natural healing process of a living creature, to use actual Medicine actions and dice-rolling rather than performing completely magical blessings, and to <i>bleed</i>. That's a lot of barriers in the way of &quot;wish really hard to turn a mountain into a palace&quot;. Likewise, I would have Clay-Wetting Practice require you to spill your blood on once-living materials [wood, bone, leather] in order to improve your Craft-based repair or manufacturing rolls... not because these materials instantly shape themselves according to your will, but because you're reanimating them and enabling them to &quot;heal&quot; themselves as you put them back together.<br /> <br /> And notice how very similar the Lunar process of healing and crafting seems, in those suggestions? That's the nature of Lunar themes and Attribute-basing working together to create an entirely different Charm tree structure than the Solars have. Solar Craft Charms and Medicine Charms are very firmly separate, but for a Lunar, they're easily all just Intelligence Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:38:40-08:00","id":805005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=804922#post804922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most uniquely Lunar Charms are the ones that give you partial transformations. Hybrid Body Rearrangement is the wrong way to go in adding mutations; Lunar Charms should mostly resemble mutations but be much more effective, and normal mutations shouldn't be the things they mess around with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I can get behind this.<br /> <br /> The Supernatural Merits of the new corebook are designed for HUMANS and humanoid things. They're not meant to be applied to wolves and eagles and whales.<br /> <br /> It would be kind of neat if the Lunar Charm for growing wings in ANY form would be part of the Lunar Strength-based Jumping Charm tree. Ideally, it would also have some synergistic effect when used with a form that already HAS wings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=804931#post804931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said this a long time ago, but I feel that a big part of the problem isn't just the lack of uniquely Lunar <i>charms</i>; the problem is that the basic Lunar narrative is very close to the Solar one, in terms of how they Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Edition has already apparently taken a baby step in the direction of distinguishing the Lunar narrative from the Solar narrative. The &quot;Luna only randomly Exalts those people who desire freedom more than life&quot; note that recurs in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Also, the potential consequences (and opportunities!) that come from starting out Casteless and needing some way of locking in a Caste, because your Exaltation is such that creating entirely new Castes is <i>possible</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:39:41-08:00","id":805026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=805000#post805000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, at least half of all Lunar Charms aren't actually more versatile than Solar ones. The Stamina Attribute in particular is thematically indistinguishable from the Resistance Ability, enabling all of the same kind of Charms and very few different concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree. I mean, I agree with your point, just not that Stamina is the best example. The Dexterity attribute is full of charms that are extremely similar to Solar charms (to the extent of frequently literally having the exact same effect, just a different cost). But Stamina has regeneration, growing giant bone spikes, hibernation, and so on. And most of all, the poison resistance/production tree. The Full Moon in my game can piss a wide variety of drugs on command; medical, recreational, or poisonous. A Solar with resistance can't do that.<br /> <br /> Stamina's actually one of my favourite Lunar charmsets... pity my Lunar doesn't favour it (of course, like all Lunar trees, there are parts I ignore so don't really think about).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-10-2016, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:59:28-08:00","id":805036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=805000#post805000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now, Flesh-Sculpting Art and Clay-Wetting Practice can still can work, by playing to Lunar themes. For example, feeding your blood to a patient blurs the boundaries of &quot;internal / external&quot;, and introduces the limitation that improving your effect upon the world requires you to work with the natural healing process of a living creature, to use actual Medicine actions and dice-rolling rather than performing completely magical blessings, and to <i>bleed</i>. That's a lot of barriers in the way of &quot;wish really hard to turn a mountain into a palace&quot;. Likewise, I would have Clay-Wetting Practice require you to spill your blood on once-living materials [wood, bone, leather] in order to improve your Craft-based repair or manufacturing rolls... not because these materials instantly shape themselves according to your will, but because you're reanimating them and enabling them to &quot;heal&quot; themselves as you put them back together.<br /> <br /> And notice how very similar the Lunar process of healing and crafting seems, in those suggestions? That's the nature of Lunar themes and Attribute-basing working together to create an entirely different Charm tree structure than the Solars have. Solar Craft Charms and Medicine Charms are very firmly separate, but for a Lunar, they're easily all just Intelligence Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really a fan of blood use to skirt normal thematic limitations, or limiting them to once-living materials. Those Charms were the ones that I hated in execution and concept, both. I'd rather see actual internal changes used than try to externalize the Lunar-ness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T23:08:03-08:00","id":805042,"title":"","content":"I liked them, because doing stuff with the blood also fits their bestial and savage themes (same as cannibalism to get shapes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:05:20-08:00","id":805106,"title":"","content":"One of the things that seemed to be touched on in 2nd ed DB charms is more cost effective charms in exchange for them being conditional. The best example off the top of my head is comparing DB's Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique, with the Solar's Spirit-Detecting Glance. SDG at 3 motes lets you sense dematerialized beings in your vicinity unconditionally, while SDMT uses only 2 motes, but only allows such detection through reflected surfaces.<br /> <br /> I really like that distinction, that while DBs are powerful much of their capability has limitations that need to be worked around, whereas Solars just hit the &quot;yes&quot; button and if need be, throw motes at the problem to yes even harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10886-maph1","name":"Maph1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:06:00-08:00","id":805107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms#post804701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar charms are technically better at doing what their ability wants you to do, and Neighborhood Relocation Technique isn't exactly going to help you against an orichalcum daiklave to the face,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why the Sidereals have Blade of the Battle Maiden, Defense of Shining Joy, Impeding the Flow, etc.<br /> <br /> For Lunars, I actually felt like Irked's Lunars homebrew conversation was actually pretty good in terms of tone, and the sort of things I'd like to see Lunars able to do - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-charms-for-3e</a>. I'd disregard some of the &quot;terrifying&quot; fluff bits because I'm not so interested in a characters who manipulates through terror so much, but they work without them.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's totally possible for Lunars to totally avoid Charms which are lensed around Abilities to some degree, because the game's systems are lensed around Abilities, and for Lunars (or any Exalted) to get Charms which ignore the base system to raise alternative Ability free mechanics in their place would be weird. You just want to stress the Attribute side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:29:24-08:00","id":805226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=805036#post805036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really a fan of blood use to skirt normal thematic limitations, or limiting them to once-living materials. Those Charms were the ones that I hated in execution and concept, both. I'd rather see actual internal changes used than try to externalize the Lunar-ness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you also want to abandon Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique, or any other method of a Lunar gifting (or cursing) someone else with a transformation into one of the Lunar's forms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:42:07-08:00","id":805232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=805226#post805226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you also want to abandon Lunar Blood Reshaping Technique, or any other method of a Lunar gifting (or cursing) someone else with a transformation into one of the Lunar's forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be nice, I suppose. Alternately, the Lunar might have to work through those in a very roundabout matter, likely involving spirits in some manner, or perhaps through a more infection-based scheme (obviously, the latter wouldn't work so well for trying to reshape objects).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:52:15-08:00","id":805239,"title":"","content":"I'm very interested to see how Lunar versatility works out in 3e. A lot of this in 2e came from only having 9 excellencies instead of 25, but this seems far less important now that those things are free anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:00:38-08:00","id":805247,"title":"","content":"well, the lunar sta charms vs solar resistance charms - ya - though I would argue that that was more due to the general lack of there not being a fundamental difference between the definition of the two<br /> <br /> I think most lunar sta charms are perfectly fitting for the concept. solar resistance charms... a bit less so - but again, it sort of depends on you interpret and define the concept of resistance as a learned skill<br /> <br /> EDIT: and yes - I am very curious to see how 3E lunars will work mechanically. With the 2.5 combo rework, then things like fury charms became instantly obsolete, outside of a few mote discounts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T09:38:02-08:00","id":805302,"title":"","content":"Going back to Charms that let Lunars partially shapeshift, what kinds of transformations are even appropriate, and how many of them are there?<br /> <br /> <br /> Sense-Sharpening Change, Armor-Forming Technique, Claws of the Silver Moon (or Scimitar Claw Technique), Bull Head Attack (for horns and charging attacks instead of claws and normal attacks), Startling Tentacle Attack, Flying Tiger Technique (flying squirrel skin-flaps), &quot;Grow Wings Prana&quot;...<br /> <br /> Growing extra humanoid arms would be appropriate for human and humanoid (or primate) forms, but clashes with more animalistic forms in terms of style and aesthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:02:19-08:00","id":806366,"title":"","content":"Sunder - good point. The specifically shape-altering charms were a bit messy that way around<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that 3E's lunars will clear that up.<br /> <br /> Though, IMO I wouldn't mind being able to go either way: Give lunars who go 'purely' animal shapes some kind of 'purity' bonus, for not sullying their forms... with the other option being going cthulhu multi-shaped, with all the flexibility and body-horror that comes with it.<br /> <br /> Like, I liked the un-tattoo'd lunar limitation on shapeshifting: if you did it too much, something would... stick - but that instantly vanished when you got inked, and even those could be veiled with a rather simple charm, making the whole &quot;you are now a walking silvery anathema beacon&quot; rather moot imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T18:23:04-08:00","id":806641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=806366#post806366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunder - good point. The specifically shape-altering charms were a bit messy that way around<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that 3E's lunars will clear that up.<br /> <br /> Though, IMO I wouldn't mind being able to go either way: Give lunars who go 'purely' animal shapes some kind of 'purity' bonus, for not sullying their forms... with the other option being going cthulhu multi-shaped, with all the flexibility and body-horror that comes with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>(rolls up a newspaper)<br /> <br /> Wait, those are hard to find...<br /> <br /> (rolls up an old copy of the Book of Shadows)<br /> <br /> There we are. No, bad webkilla, no biscuit! Lunars should never have been anywhere in the proximity of whatever Lovecraftian brainstorm that 2e had. Their concept goes against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, I liked the un-tattoo'd lunar limitation on shapeshifting: if you did it too much, something would... stick - but that instantly vanished when you got inked, and even those could be veiled with a rather simple charm, making the whole &quot;you are now a walking silvery anathema beacon&quot; rather moot imo. </div> </div> </div>Punishment for using powers is, similarly, another 2e feature that needs to be unlearned by as many people as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:00:54-08:00","id":806980,"title":"","content":"saur - I meant using stuff like hybrid body and whatnot to create shit that is decidedly unnatural. Have a stag that sprouts tentacles and have hooves with claws and bug-plate armor and scales and and wings<br /> <br /> that kind of freaky shit where you look at it and go &quot;nope.avi&quot;<br /> <br /> that kind of stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T08:50:54-08:00","id":809618,"title":"","content":"I've had an idea for a while of a Perception or Intelligence Charm that allows a Lunar to &quot;scent&quot; a person in some manner, such as getting a taste of their blood, that gives them a powerful sense of which direction they're in.<br /> <br /> Thinking of the mechanics, I had a thought of it having motes committed indefinitely, but the commitment is reduced for every scene you spend actually pursuing the quarry, to some reasonable limit.<br /> <br /> Something inspired a bit by that old image of a Tyrant Lizard that could follow a scent across a Direction. Possibly the kind of thing that might show how powers inspired by beasts can be more than just straightforward animal powers.<br /> <br /> It had a follow up Charm in which having the target's scent, or engaging in some other action to stalk them, can give you bonuses to Intelligence actions to make plans against them (whether that be coming up with strategies to destroy them, counter their own endeavours, or even just play the trickster with them).<br /> <br /> I would find such things to be distinctly Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:06:01-08:00","id":809970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=806641#post806641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Punishment for using powers is, similarly, another 2e feature that needs to be unlearned by as many people as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoyed my Lunar turning into a feathered, furry guy with weird owl eyes and odd markings, but I can get why people don't like it.<br /> <br /> Currently my mutation pool is at 40 dice, from a high of 62. I recently learnt, from re-reading the book, that the mutation pool can give you a maximum of one abomination and one deformity, so I might collect my mutations soon before we convert to 3rd ed (in case the ST decides Lunars in 3rd no longer become Chimera). Or a single derangement! (Max level of course)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-15-2016, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:39:48-08:00","id":809996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=806980#post806980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">saur - I meant using stuff like hybrid body and whatnot to create shit that is decidedly unnatural. Have a stag that sprouts tentacles and have hooves with claws and bug-plate armor and scales and and wings<br /> <br /> that kind of freaky shit where you look at it and go &quot;nope.avi&quot;<br /> <br /> that kind of stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really freaky, just the result of using a bunch of Charms to catch others off-guard. At least, it isn't freaky to Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T11:11:46-08:00","id":810297,"title":"","content":"I meant freaky to 'normal' humans and whatnot. If you're used to just being a biped with 2 arms and only 1 head... seeing someone sprout all kinds of shit is bound to be freaky","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T18:20:13-08:00","id":810434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/804701-uniquely-lunar-charms?p=810297#post810297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant freaky to 'normal' humans and whatnot. If you're used to just being a biped with 2 arms and only 1 head... seeing someone sprout all kinds of shit is bound to be freaky</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly moreso than bursting into flame, definitely not moreso than exuding an aura of blackness that actually drives you to gouge your own eyes out.<br /> <br /> Also, there are <i>already</i> stags made out of white tentacles - <i>they're a kind of demon</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-16-2016, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T23:42:38-08:00","id":810998,"title":"","content":"all the more reason for ordinary mortals to think that a lunar who does stuff like that is in fact a demon<br /> <br /> ...and everyone knows that DBs burst into flame. that's normal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}